Next step

Step 1 — Residual Add into your VPU. It's a one-line change almost, and unblocks correct transformer dataflow immediately.
Step 2 — GELU replacement for ReLU. Implement as a piecewise linear LUT in BRAM. You can swap it into your existing activation slot in the VPU.
Step 3 — Layer Normalization. Build as a two-pass unit: first pass accumulates mean and variance across the vector, second pass normalizes and applies γ/β using your existing scale/bias hardware.
Step 4 — Transpose addressing for K matrix. No new compute, just address generation logic so your MAC array can consume K in transposed order.
Step 5 — Attention score buffer. A BRAM block to hold the [seq_len × seq_len] intermediate matrix between QKᵀ and the softmax.
Step 6 — Softmax Unit. The most complex addition. Build it last so you can test everything else independently first.


Embedding Fetch Unit
Parameters:
  EMBEDDING_DIM  = 768
  ELEM_WIDTH     = 8        // INT8
  DDR_BASE_WTE   = address of wte in DDR
  DDR_BASE_WPE   = address of wpe in BRAM or DDR

Ports:
  input  [15:0]   token_ids   [SEQ_LEN]   // input token sequence
  input  [9:0]    seq_len                 // actual sequence length
  output [7:0]    embed_out   [SEQ_LEN][768]  // to activation buffer
  input           start
  output          done







